<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Kongo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kongo Empire, Kongo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of Kongo was a Central African state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbanza-kongo">Mbanza Kongo</a> in present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, flourishing from the fourteenth century. It entered into contact with Portugal in the 1480s, and its rulers adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. Its history, covered in the Kongo Empire profile, was shaped by trade, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a> and conflict with the Portuguese.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Kongo" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oren neu dag · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Kongo_according_to_Giovanni_Cavazzi_da_Montecuccolo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
